From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 03:00:00 -0700
Subject: cam: icp: skip FW MEM_MAP/UNMAP unsupported by sdm845 firmware

The sdm845-era ICP firmware (CICP.FW.1.0-00050, 2018) predates the
HFI_IPEBPS_CMD_OPCODE_MEM_MAP/UNMAP opcodes camera_kt sends around the
io-config stage of BPS/IPE acquire: the FW debug queue logs
"IB_DM: Unrecognized opcode 0x0000000e at ipebpsdomain.c:1278" and never
responds, so the 5 s wait in cam_icp_process_stream_settings fails the
whole acquire ("sending config io mapping failed rc -110"). The legacy
4.9 driver never sends MEM_MAP; the io-config regions are delivered via
the CONFIG_IO async command which this FW handles. Make
cam_icp_process_stream_settings a no-op.
---

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
index 8c98e0d..ed38387 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
@@ -4377,6 +4377,20 @@ static int cam_icp_process_stream_settings(
 	struct hfi_cmd_ipe_bps_map  *map_cmd;
 	struct hfi_cmd_ipebps_async *async_direct;
 
+	/*
+	 * The sdm845-era ICP firmware (CICP.FW.1.0-00050) predates the
+	 * HFI_IPEBPS_CMD_OPCODE_MEM_MAP/UNMAP opcodes (0xe/0xf) and rejects
+	 * them ("Unrecognized opcode 0x0000000e"), never responding - the
+	 * 5 s wait then fails the whole acquire. The io-config regions are
+	 * delivered via the CONFIG_IO async command instead, as on the
+	 * legacy 4.9 driver which never sends MEM_MAP. Skip it.
+	 */
+	if (map_unmap)
+		CAM_DBG(CAM_ICP, "skipping FW MEM_MAP (unsupported by FW)");
+	else
+		CAM_DBG(CAM_ICP, "skipping FW MEM_UNMAP (unsupported by FW)");
+	return 0;
+
 	map_cmd_size =
 		sizeof(struct hfi_cmd_ipe_bps_map) +
 		((cmd_mem_regions->num_regions - 1) *
